The type alias ``VALUE`` in ``qcodes.dataset.sqlite.query_helpers`` now includes
the numpy integer, floating point and complex scalar types. These are already
supported at runtime by ``DataSet.add_results`` and the other functions that
store data in the database, so passing numpy scalars to them no longer produces a
type checking error. Since ``VALUE`` is also used as the return type of methods
such as ``DataSet.get_metadata``, code that annotates the returned values may
need to handle numpy scalar types too.
